{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>At that time</b> — תשרת בעבור אחרת ובעת ההיא בקבצי אתכם ותחסר אות בי״ת ובי״ת בעת תשרת, בעבור אחרת בקבצי. This is the opinion of R. Moses. And there is no need." "<b>Your captivity</b> — like ושבית שביתיך בתוכהנה (and I will turn your captivity within her)." "<b>Before your eyes</b> — in your eyes you will see. This is what HaShem said. Our predecessors of blessed memory joined these twelve books and counted them as one book in the reckoning of twenty-four books, because the books are small and they are of one purport, for all of them are future prophecies. The Five Megillot are not so, for Lamentations is the opposite of Song of Songs. And because Zephaniah lived in the days of Josiah, they placed him ninth, for the others were after the Babylonian exile."], :book :zephaniah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The citation of R. Moses Ha-Kohen appears to propose a metathesis of letters across word boundaries; the passage is highly compressed and the exact reference is uncertain.", 2 "Resolved וקדמונינו ז״ל as 'our predecessors of blessed memory'; the sentence 'This is what HaShem said' may mark the close of the prophetic corpus or refer back to the verse, and is rendered literally without further gloss."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zephaniah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zfanya"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:47:38.316528149Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}